# === Vendored third-party sources (regenerate via scripts) ===
#
# Why vendor/ is ignored: the sqlite3 amalgamation (~10 MB of binary-like
# C data), the MinGW symlink farm at vendor/sqlite3/libc-windows-amd64/
# (~2 552 symlinks), the prebuilt libsqlite3.a / libcurl.a archives for
# each target, and the Windows libcurl-x64.dll are all very large and
# bloat every `git clone` / `git checkout`. They can be regenerated
# from a fresh checkout by running the bootstrap scripts:
#
#   bash scripts/fetch-vendor-sqlite3.sh   # downloads amalgamation + builds libsqlite3.a
#   bash scripts/build-vendor-curl.sh      # cross-compiles libcurl.a per target
#   bash scripts/build-vendor-mingw.sh     # regenerates MinGW symlink farm for Windows
#
# The build.zig checks for these on first invocation and prints a clear
# error if any are missing — see the scripts/ directory for details.
/vendor/

